<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ FBT prescribed rate falls to 9.65 percent.</title>
<headline>NZ FBT prescribed rate falls to 9.65 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance Minister Bill Birch said on Tuesday the rate of interest used to calculate the fringe benefit value of low-interest employment-related loans had been cut to 9.65 percent from 10 percent for the quarter starting April 1.</p>
<p>Birch said the new rate reflected the recent fall in market rates.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
